tour feature-comment-reply
kind flow
author ai
group features/cli
note The agent, after doing what a comment asked and putting the explanation in the map, at the moment the human must learn that it was done and where to read it. Goal: the human reads the map instead of the diff, so the answer points into the map rather than into the chat. Without this command the answer lives only in the agent's transcript, which the human may have closed and which is not beside the code the question was about. A change to the note the comment sits on cannot stand in for the reply: a comment on code has no note, a fix may land in another tour, and only the reply says which. It writes the reply into the comment's file at once; an open window reads the store again within a second, turns the box green with the reply under the question and counts it in the top bar until the human dismisses it (the GUI scenario 'comments' replies from the Console and dumps the answered box). A second reply replaces the first, so after follow-up work the human reads the current answer, not a thread. An unknown id or an empty reply is refused. Why comments exist and the designs that were tried are in feature-add-comment.

